  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return of an individual in the Philippines is on or before April 15 of the following year after the close of the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their income tax returns are filed by April 15 to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to prepare and submit the return well in advance of the deadline to ensure compliance and to address any potential issues that may arise during the filing process.",
